Description: audio player with playlists, CUE sheets, LED meters and spectrum analyser
 Linux Aurora Player (a fork of Sonora) is an Audacious-style audio player built with Qt 6 and GStreamer.
 Features: any number of playlists with artist/album/year/time/type columns
 and metadata tooltips, per-playlist filter, CUE sheet support (cue + FLAC
 and other images), playlist import/export (M3U, PLS, XSPF), LED level
 meters with true-peak detection, a configurable spectrum analyser that is
 synchronised with the sound, selectable sound service (PipeWire,
 PulseAudio, ALSA, JACK, ...) and output device, dark mode, and MPRIS2
 support so that the keyboard's dedicated media keys work.
